  "rationale": "The requirement is met. It asks for a Cargo integration test in the Habeas crate that calls `habeas::validate()` on its own project.\n\n- **The test exists.** `tests/habeas.rs` has a `#[test] fn habeas()` that calls `habeas::validate()`. Cargo auto-discovers it as an integration test, and `Cargo.toml` has no `[[test]]` or `autotests` override that would disable it. The test carries a `{test}` reference to `requirements.integration.self_test`.\n- **It checks the project itself.** `validate()` in `src/lib.rs` (lines 26–49) finds the nearest ancestor of the current directory that has both `Cargo.toml` and `book.toml`. For `cargo test` in this crate, that is the Habeas project. It then runs `validate_repository` on that root and panics if the report has any errors. A passing test therefore means the project's own requirements and evidence validate.\n- **No `{impl}` is missing.** The requirement asks for a test, so the test is the implementation. `validate()` is marked as implementing `requirements.integration.validate`, which is a different definition, and it adds no behavior beyond that.\n- **Test coverage is sufficient.** The requirement is a single behavior, and the test exercises it end to end. Nothing else in the design space needs a separate test.",
